  "question": {
    "text": "An electric toaster has resistance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo> </mo><mi>Ω</mi></math> at room temperature <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>27</mn><mo> </mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. The toaster is connected to a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>220</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> supply. If the current flowing through it reaches <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>75</mn><mo> </mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>, the temperature attained by toaster is around: (if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><none></none><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mo>∘</mo></mmultiscripts></math> )",
    "image": null
  },
